		<dc:title id="title">Beautiful Stories from Shakespeare</dc:title>
		<meta property="file-as" refines="#title">Beautiful Stories from Shakespeare</meta>
		<dc:subject id="subject-1">Children's literature</dc:subject>
		<meta property="authority" refines="#subject-1">LCSH</meta>
		<meta property="term" refines="#subject-1">sh85023598</meta>
		<dc:subject id="subject-2">Shakespeare, William, 1564-1616--Stories, plots, etc.--Juvenile literature</dc:subject>
		<meta property="authority" refines="#subject-2">LCSH</meta>
		<meta property="term" refines="#subject-2">Unknown</meta>
		<meta property="schema:genre">Children’s</meta>
		<meta property="schema:abstract">Retellings of Shakespeare’s plays for young readers.</meta>
		<dc:description>
			&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/e-nesbit"&gt;E. Nesbit&lt;/a&gt; was an English writer who published numerous books for children. &lt;i&gt;Beautiful Stories from Shakespeare&lt;/i&gt; is a collection of short prose retellings of twenty of &lt;a href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/william-shakespeare"&gt;Shakespeare’s&lt;/a&gt; plays. E. Nesbit condensed the stories to ensure they are understood by children and that children will find them entertaining. Some Shakespearean language is retained, but the emphasis is on the story.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;The American edition, edited by E. T. Roe, includes a short biography of Shakespeare, a pronunciation guide for names and a list of famous Shakespearean quotations grouped by theme.&lt;/p&gt;
		</dc:description>
